WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.220
A good share of a federal estate sits
outside Arc's support list: the Unix systems,

2
00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.625
and several older Linux releases that stop
getting new agent versions in late 2026.

3
00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:14.963
Those are tier two, and Ansible
reaches them over S S H.

4
00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:16.126
Two cautions.

5
00:00:16.126 --> 00:00:19.650
Privilege escalation can't be
narrowed to specific commands,

6
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:24.350
so that account has broad rights and has
to be governed like a privileged identity.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:29.288
And check mode is only a simulation, so
each drift check should stand on its own.

8
00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:31.625
Network gear is the easy win.

9
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:34.205
A read-only facts run gives you the model,

10
00:00:34.205 --> 00:00:38.037
serial and version of every
device, with nothing installed.

11
00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.710
Where a vendor controller exists,
it owns the configuration.
